{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"goofy-disquieted-pheasant","creation_channel":"cli","description":"S2 (e042) ReconcilerSettings captures comment_max_chars and jira_cli_timeout at compose, but neither is threaded into the built backend/DC sanitizer — the DC sanitizer's comment_max_chars() still calls resolve_comment_max_chars() ambiently. Thread the captured values through so the DC comment sanitizer uses the compose-captured value (completing the operation-scoped capture for these two fields), or drop the unused capture. Advisory finding from Gerrit 1843 PS1 LLM-Review.","id":"2048-d289-e55f-4595","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 follow-up: thread captured comment_max_chars/jira_cli_timeout into the built reconciler backend/sanitizer"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787024834647530001,"uuid":"fc9a8ee6-47dc-45cb-9c66-bdbcd7a1772c"}